-- title:
--   Localising at n over a reduced Artinian fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $C$ be a commutative local ring and $C'$ a commutative $C$-algebra, and write $M' := \mathfrak m_C C' = (\mathrm{maximalIdeal}\,C).\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\ C\ C')$ for the ideal of $C'$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $C$. Let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $C'$ containing $M'$, and assume the closed fibre $C'/M'$ is reduced and Artinian. Put $D := \mathrm{Localization.AtPrime}\ \mathfrak n$, the localisation of $C'$ at $\mathfrak n$, viewed as a $C$-algebra by composition. The conclusion is a conjunction of four assertions: (i) the ideal of $D$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_C$ equals the maximal ideal of $D$; (ii) the structure map $C \to D$ is a local homomorphism, i.e. it reflects units; (iii) the composite of $C' \to D$ with the residue map $D \to D/\mathfrak m_D$ is surjective; and (iv) the kernel of that composite is exactly $\mathfrak n$. Together (iii) and (iv) identify the residue field of $D$ with $C'/\mathfrak n$.
--
--   This is the statement that localising $C'$ at a maximal ideal above $\mathfrak m_C$ is unramified over $C$ when the closed fibre is reduced and Artinian, together with the identification of the residue field of the localisation with $C'/\mathfrak n$. It is used in the construction of a faithfully flat local extension of an Artinian ring with algebraically closed residue field, where controlling $\mathfrak m_C D = \mathfrak m_D$ is what preserves smallness of surjections after base change.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_map_maximalIdeal_eq_maximalIdeal_localization_atPrime_of_isReduced_of_isArtinianRing.lean

import Mathlib

